      },
      "text": "The digital photography workflow is a signal chain from captured photons to final output. Every step is a transformation of image data, and understanding what information exists at each stage — and what irreversibly destroys it — determines the quality ceiling of the final image. The critical insight is that RAW preserves all captured information; everything downstream narrows the information available to you."
    },
